  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-11T17:00:16.259Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Similar to how web browsers will prompt you to give microphone/webcam permissions to a web page. Or how smart phones will prompt you to give location access to apps.\nSome Worlds need particular configurations of the VRChat client in order to be most effective. The most common examples are World audio level and hide/show nameplates.\nPlease add controls in the Player API to display a prompt to a player with a list of access requests for the World. Ideally those configuration options could revert automatically.\nWe especially need controls like these for VR live theater and roleplay worlds.\nFor scenarios like that, we also need somewhat more demanding config changes from the audience, including disabling the \"Personal Space\" setting. That's a little bit more dangerous to add to the player API, so I'd suggest separating \"Requested\" configurations and \"Suggested\" configurations. But that's up to design.\nRelated: https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/add-a-force-nameplates-off-feature-to-the-player-api",
